t":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99480","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99480","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99480.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99480.patch","merged_at":"2024-12-03T20:47:26Z"},"body":"Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/9369\r\n\r\nThis PR makes the external links in the built-in class reference:\r\n- Display with an \"external link\" icon\r\n- Coloured differently than surrounding text\r\n- Without outline unless hovered on\r\n- With a tooltip containing the link\r\n\r\nI'm unconvinced on the actual color, though. See also a [RocketChat thread](https://chat.godotengine.org/channel/documentation/thread/YSvnSkorpFYy7Gu8M). The gist of it is that, I feel like the excessive accent colour brings too much attention to external links, and the icon exists too. Links to the **built-in** class reference are more important in the editor and should be more notable, as well.\r\n\r\n| Normal Link Color | Saturated Link Color |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| ![thumb-Clipboard - November 20, 2024 8_08 PM](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0f336761-7849-41c0-b416-61820546de79) | ![thumb-Clipboard - November 20, 2024 8_13 PM](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dbdbd9d7-99ac-427c-954f-41b3514ee853) |\r\n| ![Clipboard - November 20, 2024 8_08 PM](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bc46420b-9406-42d0-9a72-3f11492855e8) | ![Clipboard - November 20, 2024 8_14 PM](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/542a5c38-51b8-4c15-bc3e-a1dc08d70e45)\r\n\r\nIt's also currently not possible to hide the `hint` tag's underline individually. Hence the dotted underline on these links.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","follow